alleries Mission Galleries 35th Anniversary Galleries Media Resources FEATURED IMAGE TOUR Trifid Nebula Tour NASA is celebrated Hubble's 36th anniversary with a stunning new look at the Trifid Nebula, a star-forming region about 5,000 light-years away. First imaged in 1997, Hubble revisited this scene nearly 30 years later with sharper vision. The image reveals a structure nicknamed the “Cosmic Sea Slug,” including a jet from Herbig-Haro 399, showing how young stars actively shape their surroundings. Hubble Senior Project Scientist, Dr. Jennifer Wiseman takes us on a tour of this beautiful image. Learn More Search Hubble Images Type Hubble Fridays H","dup":0,"failed":0}
